Existing playbook:
ACE Playbook Insights
Use these distilled reminders to plan tool usage. Keep tool calls faithful to the functions provided in the BFCL benchmark.

message_api
- delta1: State-modifying operations (set_user_id, contact_customer_support) must invoke immediately when intent is clear; do not defer for missing context.
- delta2: Distinguish parameter-setting statements (user ID, preferences) from context-only remarks; parameter statements must trigger state-update tool calls.
- delta3: Use provided recipient identifiers (names, user IDs) directly in send_message; avoid exploratory list_users/get_user_id calls when recipient is explicit.

vehicle_control_api
- delta1: Execute all state-modifying tool calls immediately when identified as necessary—don't defer or suggest; invoke pressBrakePedal, set_navigation, and similar operations as explicit calls, not conversational recommendations.
- delta2: In multi-turn sequences, complete prerequisite operations (e.g., brake pedal before engine start) before proceeding to next user request. Verify state transitions are reflected in tool calls, not just dialogue.
- delta3: When recommending a destination (tire shop, location), immediately call set_navigation with the address rather than asking permission. State consistency requires the navigation call to execute in the same turn.

